Description: Desktop environment
 Common desktop infrastructure — Xorg, audio (ALSA), printing
 (CUPS), network discovery (Avahi/mDNS), font fallback for emoji
 (Symbola), and xdg-utils for desktop integration.  Mirrors the
 content of config/pkg.list [desktop] — keep in sync when adding/
 removing packages.  Today `gnome-desktop` pulls Xorg via its own
 Key list, so selecting this task alongside `gnome-desktop` is
 mostly redundant.
